# u-forge.ai — Repository Rules

u-forge.ai is a local-first TTRPG worldbuilding tool with a Rust/GPUI desktop UI
and a SQLite knowledge graph. Inference through Lemonade is optional:
`KnowledgeGraph` and the desktop's graph features must work with no server or
environment overrides.

[ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) explains the workspace, subsystem boundaries,
and design decisions. Read the topic guides that apply to the change:

| Task | Local contract |
| --- | --- |
| Builds, setup, releases | [BUILD.md](BUILD.md) |
| Configuration, runtime discovery, XDG paths | [Environment and configuration](.rulesdir/environment-config.mdc) |
| Tracked work, issue intake, PRs, hosted CI | [Repository workflow](.rulesdir/development-workflow.mdc) |
| Tests and fixtures | [Testing and debugging](.rulesdir/testing-debugging.mdc) |
| Rust, storage, queue lifetimes, or application agent prompts/tools | [Rust patterns](.rulesdir/rust-patterns.mdc) |
| Wiring inference or changing startup/model selection | [Integration boundaries](.rulesdir/project-structure.mdc) and [Rust patterns](.rulesdir/rust-patterns.mdc) |
| GPUI rendering, interaction, or window chrome | [GPUI patterns](.rulesdir/gpui-patterns.mdc) |
| Schemas (`defaults/schemas/`) and validation | [Schema system](.rulesdir/schema-system.mdc) |
| JSONL (`defaults/data/`), conversion, or data import | [JSON data formats](.rulesdir/json-data-formats.mdc) and [Schema system](.rulesdir/schema-system.mdc) |

`make test` is the canonical full suite; it owns a pinned Lemonade runtime.
`make test-ci` is the graph-only suite, not a substitute for live coverage.
